From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sckiyo <sckiyo@outlook.com>
Date: Sat Sep 19 12:00:00 2026 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: overlay: build dshanpi-r1 AP62xx overlay

The .dts itself is copied in via the overlay-directories mechanism
(0000.patching_config.yaml); only register it here. Vendor 6.1 builds
overlays from %.dts, not %.dtso. Do not ship an overlay/Makefile in
the patch directory: copy_bare_files would overwrite the vendor tree's
shared overlay Makefile (~350 entries used by every rk35xx board).

A second dtbo- += assignment is inserted in front of dtbotxt-, instead
of extending the last entry of the existing list. Upstream appending
another overlay does not change the dtbotxt block, so the patch still
applies.

Signed-off-by: sckiyo <sckiyo@outlook.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/overlay/Makefile | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/overlay/Makefile b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/overlay/Makefile
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/overlay/Makefile
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/overlay/Makefile
@@ -356,2 +356,4 @@
+dtbo-$(CONFIG_ARCH_ROCKCHIP) += rk3568-dshanpi-r1-wlan-ap6256.dtbo
+
 dtbotxt-$(CONFIG_ARCH_ROCKCHIP) += \
 	README.rockchip-overlays
--
2.39.5
